<code>assert !this.empty() => \result == this.get(this.size() - 1);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the stack is not empty (`!this.empty()`), then the result of the `peek` method (`\result`) is equal to the last item in the stack (`this.get(this.size() - 1)`). Since the problem specifies that the stack can contain `null` values, we don't need to handle the case where the result is `null` separately, as the equality check will naturally cover that scenario.
